BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Compute Runs on Minerals: Mapping AI’s Critical Mineral Exposure
  in the Age of Pax Silica
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T210000
UID:evt-C9UC5Ur3ANr8SF9@events.lu.ma
DESCRIPTION:Address:\nCheck event page for more details.\n\nEvery frontier
  model runs on minerals. Behind the GPUs\, the servers\, the cooling syste
 ms and the power infrastructure that make up a data centre sit gallium\, g
 ermanium\, rare earths\, copper\, tungsten and a dozen other inputs whose 
 mining and refining are concentrated in a small number of countries. Count
 ries like China\, that have weaponized that dominance\, restricting export
 s of gallium\, germanium\, graphite and rare earth magnets\, and each time
  targeting a material critical to AI. Demonstrating how a supply chain cho
 kepoint becomes a tool of statecraft.\n\nWhat exactly is AI infrastructure
 \,…\n\nHosted by Georgia Berg
LOCATION:https://luma.com/event/evt-C9UC5Ur3ANr8SF9
URL:https://luma.com/trajec-ozbd
X-SOURCE:Luma Toronto Discover
END:VEVENT
